Question :-
74. Search a 2D Matrix
You are given an m x n integer matrix matrix with the following two properties:

Each row is sorted in non-decreasing order.
The first integer of each row is greater than the last integer of the previous row.
Given an integer target, return true if target is in matrix or false otherwise.

You must write a solution in O(log(m * n)) time complexity.

Explanation :-
The main challenge and restriction is to solve this under the time complexity - log(m*n). The key idea is to visualize the matrix as a 1-D array and access elements
by using 'mid/n' and 'mid%n' after 'mid's updation.
Refer to the code for better understanding

Solution :-
class Solution {
public:
    bool searchMatrix(vector<vector<int>>& matrix, int target) {
        int m=matrix.size(),n=matrix[0].size();
        int low=0,high=m*n-1,mid=0;
        while(low<=high){
            mid = low + (high-low/2);
            if(target==matrix[mid/n][mid%n]){
                return 1;
            }
            else if(target<matrix[mid/n][mid%n]){
                high=mid-1;
            }
            else{
                low= mid+1;
            }
        }
        return 0;   
    }
};

here updation is done as if we are using a 1-D array yet the only change is the accessing of middle value for which we use division and remainder on mid variable.
